    {
      "id": 422,
      "name": "Introduction to Data Science and Its Workflow",
      "type": "general",
      "blocksVersion": "v2",
      "blocks": [],
      "blocksV2": [
        {
          "id": "9c9e0fd2-f9c4-4fa7-8ee9-7babb8376525",
          "type": "heading",
          "props": {
            "level": 1,
            "textColor": "default",
            "isToggleable": false,
            "textAlignment": "left",
            "backgroundColor": "default"
          },
          "content": [
            {
              "text": "What Is Data Science?",
              "type": "text",
              "styles": {}
            }
          ],
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "id": "9591f9a1-600e-4d53-b106-fb7b50bc20da",
          "type": "heading",
          "props": {
            "level": 3,
            "textColor": "default",
            "isToggleable": false,
            "textAlignment": "left",
            "backgroundColor": "default"
          },
          "content": [
            {
              "text": "Overview",
              "type": "text",
              "styles": {}
            }
          ],
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "id": "67f3a95a-785f-4147-b222-8ac4fbd31127",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "props": {
            "textColor": "default",
            "textAlignment": "left",
            "backgroundColor": "default"
          },
          "content": [
            {
              "text": "Data science is an interdisciplinary field combining domain expertise, programming, and statistics to",
              "type": "text",
              "styles": {}
            }
          ],
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "id": "9e7295e4-56ae-475c-bedf-ece6be1ed8e7",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "props": {
            "textColor": "default",
            "textAlignment": "left",
            "backgroundColor": "default"
          },
          "content": [
            {
              "text": "extract meaningful insights from data. A typical workflow follows five stages: collect, clean, explore,",
              "type": "text",
              "styles": {}
            }
          ],
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "id": "9f0705b3-95d5-4ee3-bff9-981faa813156",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "props": {
            "textColor": "default",
            "textAlignment": "left",
            "backgroundColor": "default"
          },
          "content": [
            {
              "text": "model, and communicate.",
              "type": "text",
              "styles": {}
            }
          ],
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "id": "dd9568fe-f1c3-464d-b767-3166ff6d6760",
          "type": "heading",
          "props": {
            "level": 3,
            "textColor": "default",
            "isToggleable": false,
            "textAlignment": "left",
            "backgroundColor": "default"
          },
          "content": [
            {
              "text": "The Data Science Workflow",
              "type": "text",
              "styles": {}
            }
          ],
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "id": "153b5d83-3f8f-49d4-9d98-4336c5d66b1a",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "props": {
            "textColor": "default",
            "textAlignment": "left",
            "backgroundColor": "default"
          },
          "content": [
            {
              "text": "Collect — gather raw data from APIs, databases, sensors, and surveys.",
              "type": "text",
              "styles": {}
            }
          ],
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "id": "3422a600-b9f5-4692-9180-1cdf596cee93",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "props": {
            "textColor": "default",
            "textAlignment": "left",
            "backgroundColor": "default"
          },
          "content": [
            {
              "text": "Clean — handle missing values, outliers, and formatting errors using tools like pandas.",
              "type": "text",
              "styles": {}
            }
          ],
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "id": "1dd5e076-acf4-4a3f-864a-a19dbf17008c",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "props": {
            "textColor": "default",
            "textAlignment": "left",
            "backgroundColor": "default"
          },
          "content": [
            {
              "text": "Explore — summarize distributions and correlations with matplotlib and seaborn.",
              "type": "text",
              "styles": {}
            }
          ],
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "id": "6c76833a-8d54-4e4c-a6b6-ec43a63976ab",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "props": {
            "textColor": "default",
            "textAlignment": "left",
            "backgroundColor": "default"
          },
          "content": [
            {
              "text": "Model — apply statistical or machine learning methods using scikit-learn or statsmodels.",
              "type": "text",
              "styles": {}
            }
          ],
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "id": "00e27986-270f-4a02-90d1-bb46380700e0",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "props": {
            "textColor": "default",
            "textAlignment": "left",
            "backgroundColor": "default"
          },
          "content": [
            {
              "text": "Communicate — present findings clearly using Jupyter notebooks, slides, or dashboards.",
              "type": "text",
              "styles": {}
            }
          ],
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "id": "922a0f09-e4bf-4de8-ab92-3e13ef9edad1",
          "type": "heading",
          "props": {
            "level": 3,
            "textColor": "default",
            "isToggleable": false,
            "textAlignment": "left",
            "backgroundColor": "default"
          },
          "content": [
            {
              "text": "Key Insight",
              "type": "text",
              "styles": {}
            }
          ],
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "id": "c61f6105-f977-4398-a8f2-df6595106643",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "props": {
            "textColor": "default",
            "textAlignment": "left",
            "backgroundColor": "default"
          },
          "content": [
            {
              "text": "The most impactful data scientists spend the majority of their time on the first three stages: collecting,",
              "type": "text",
              "styles": {}
            }
          ],
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "id": "95cf97f3-e60a-4686-9669-97f418cf9e8a",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "props": {
            "textColor": "default",
            "textAlignment": "left",
            "backgroundColor": "default"
          },
          "content": [
            {
              "text": "cleaning, and understanding data before a single model is trained.",
              "type": "text",
              "styles": {}
            }
          ],
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 423,
      "name": "Understanding Data Types and Variable Classification",
      "type": "general",
      "blocksVersion": "v2",
      "blocks": [],
      "blocksV2": [
        {
          "id": "dfbfc0ec-10b0-40c9-8e85-4438b569a1aa",
          "type": "heading",
          "props": {
            "level": 1,
            "textColor": "default",
            "isToggleable": false,
            "textAlignment": "left",
            "backgroundColor": "default"
          },
          "content": [
            {
              "text": "Data Types & Structures",
              "type": "text",
              "styles": {}
            }
          ],
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "id": "e4654a9e-6671-4c83-9280-e75dbed4c97a",
          "type": "heading",
          "props": {
            "level": 3,
            "textColor": "default",
            "isToggleable": false,
            "textAlignment": "left",
            "backgroundColor": "default"
          },
          "content": [
            {
              "text": "Core Concepts",
              "type": "text",
              "styles": {}
            }
          ],
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "id": "8dfce5ff-0de7-49d2-846d-4dba8b2e98f8",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "props": {
            "textColor": "default",
            "textAlignment": "left",
            "backgroundColor": "default"
          },
          "content": [
            {
              "text": "The type of variable you are working with determines which operations, visualizations, and models are",
              "type": "text",
              "styles": {}
            }
          ],
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "id": "9ab3cf25-9379-465b-89e8-9ddce4d9eb5f",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "props": {
            "textColor": "default",
            "textAlignment": "left",
            "backgroundColor": "default"
          },
          "content": [
            {
              "text": "appropriate. Treating a categorical variable as a number is one of the most common beginner mistakes.",
              "type": "text",
              "styles": {}
            }
          ],
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "id": "c8cea304-d391-48f8-a1bb-be8a359a277b",
          "type": "heading",
          "props": {
            "level": 3,
            "textColor": "default",
            "isToggleable": false,
            "textAlignment": "left",
            "backgroundColor": "default"
          },
          "content": [
            {
              "text": "Variable Types",
              "type": "text",
              "styles": {}
            }
          ],
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "id": "42896e9f-e3ee-42a2-afcf-51660dfc90b7",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "props": {
            "textColor": "default",
            "textAlignment": "left",
            "backgroundColor": "default"
          },
          "content": [
            {
              "text": "Continuous — numeric with infinite possible values (e.g. salary, temperature). Best summarized",
              "type": "text",
              "styles": {}
            }
          ],
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "id": "5e60c169-9fbd-4b19-a5bb-5ca7dbb92b11",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "props": {
            "textColor": "default",
            "textAlignment": "left",
            "backgroundColor": "default"
          },
          "content": [
            {
              "text": "with mean and standard deviation.",
              "type": "text",
              "styles": {}
            }
          ],
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "id": "546831ac-56b4-4bd5-bb58-1472e4161ff5",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "props": {
            "textColor": "default",
            "textAlignment": "left",
            "backgroundColor": "default"
          },
          "content": [
            {
              "text": "Discrete — numeric but countable (e.g. number of purchases). Use count or median.",
              "type": "text",
              "styles": {}
            }
          ],
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "id": "c4ba5882-64e0-47f4-8795-a563b9ae5b0d",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "props": {
            "textColor": "default",
            "textAlignment": "left",
            "backgroundColor": "default"
          },
          "content": [
            {
              "text": "Nominal — categories with no meaningful order (e.g. country, color). Use mode or frequency.",
              "type": "text",
              "styles": {}
            }
          ],
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "id": "35bb5669-8e7d-4b20-b1b5-e3108ba8724e",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "props": {
            "textColor": "default",
            "textAlignment": "left",
            "backgroundColor": "default"
          },
          "content": [
            {
              "text": "Ordinal — categories with a meaningful order (e.g. star ratings 1–5). Use median or rank.",
              "type": "text",
              "styles": {}
            }
          ],
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "id": "89e02779-9fbc-496e-9a6e-bfe09d7cb46a",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "props": {
            "textColor": "default",
            "textAlignment": "left",
            "backgroundColor": "default"
          },
          "content": [
            {
              "text": "Boolean — only two possible values, yes/no or true/false. Summarized as a proportion.",
              "type": "text",
              "styles": {}
            }
          ],
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "id": "1f75b274-7c01-4143-a22e-bedcfc29a42f",
          "type": "heading",
          "props": {
            "level": 3,
            "textColor": "default",
            "isToggleable": false,
            "textAlignment": "left",
            "backgroundColor": "default"
          },
          "content": [
            {
              "text": "Common Pitfall",
              "type": "text",
              "styles": {}
            }
          ],
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "id": "56be9273-1e7c-408c-92e8-68a7dc8a1717",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "props": {
            "textColor": "default",
            "textAlignment": "left",
            "backgroundColor": "default"
          },
          "content": [
            {
              "text": "Zip codes, phone numbers, and ID columns look numeric but are nominal. Always ask: does arithmetic",
              "type": "text",
              "styles": {}
            }
          ],
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "id": "9e926269-8b11-48e6-abb8-711a97510498",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "props": {
            "textColor": "default",
            "textAlignment": "left",
            "backgroundColor": "default"
          },
          "content": [
            {
              "text": "on this column make sense? If not, treat it as categorical.",
              "type": "text",
              "styles": {}
            }
          ],
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 424,
      "name": "Exploratory Data Analysis: Concepts and Techniques",
      "type": "general",
      "blocksVersion": "v2",
      "blocks": [],
      "blocksV2": [
        {
          "id": "09ce26fa-895d-491d-8134-2a6e74e7fdee",
          "type": "heading",
          "props": {
            "level": 1,
            "textColor": "default",
            "isToggleable": false,
            "textAlignment": "left",
            "backgroundColor": "default"
          },
          "content": [
            {
              "text": "Exploratory Data Analysis",
              "type": "text",
              "styles": {}
            }
          ],
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "id": "be788559-8c9f-450f-860e-d615d2a11307",
          "type": "heading",
          "props": {
            "level": 3,
            "textColor": "default",
            "isToggleable": false,
            "textAlignment": "left",
            "backgroundColor": "default"
          },
          "content": [
            {
              "text": "Core Concepts",
              "type": "text",
              "styles": {}
            }
          ],
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "id": "faa7cf3b-3776-4130-8de5-520be95ee675",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "props": {
            "textColor": "default",
            "textAlignment": "left",
            "backgroundColor": "default"
          },
          "content": [
            {
              "text": "Exploratory Data Analysis (EDA) is the process of visually and statistically summarizing a dataset",
              "type": "text",
              "styles": {}
            }
          ],
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "id": "2eb334be-b7d0-4c68-b710-af90739c36a4",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "props": {
            "textColor": "default",
            "textAlignment": "left",
            "backgroundColor": "default"
          },
          "content": [
            {
              "text": "before applying any models. The goal is to understand the shape, spread, and relationships in the data.",
              "type": "text",
              "styles": {}
            }
          ],
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "id": "d0eeb7d4-efe5-4dfc-9bab-697ecd035ad3",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "props": {
            "textColor": "default",
            "textAlignment": "left",
            "backgroundColor": "default"
          },
          "content": [
            {
              "text": "EDA was formalized by statistician John Tukey in 1977 and remains the most critical step in any",
              "type": "text",
              "styles": {}
            }
          ],
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "id": "20179225-1410-4210-8113-1c146e54d50a",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "props": {
            "textColor": "default",
            "textAlignment": "left",
            "backgroundColor": "default"
          },
          "content": [
            {
              "text": "analysis.",
              "type": "text",
              "styles": {}
            }
          ],
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "id": "98629002-d3e2-4254-b88b-8a0c7b130d14",
          "type": "heading",
          "props": {
            "level": 3,
            "textColor": "default",
            "isToggleable": false,
            "textAlignment": "left",
            "backgroundColor": "default"
          },
          "content": [
            {
              "text": "Key Visualizations",
              "type": "text",
              "styles": {}
            }
          ],
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "id": "cf238528-0ebd-4082-9064-93be51c212cd",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "props": {
            "textColor": "default",
            "textAlignment": "left",
            "backgroundColor": "default"
          },
          "content": [
            {
              "text": "Histogram — shows the distribution of a single variable. Use df[\"col\"].plot.hist() or plt.hist(df[\"col\"]).",
              "type": "text",
              "styles": {}
            }
          ],
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "id": "9c6984e5-7337-4f05-a4a1-bc885fdda67c",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "props": {
            "textColor": "default",
            "textAlignment": "left",
            "backgroundColor": "default"
          },
          "content": [
            {
              "text": "Boxplot — displays spread and highlights outliers. Use df.boxplot(column=\"col\").",
              "type": "text",
              "styles": {}
            }
          ],
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "id": "1b696ef3-5057-426a-92c8-2e38ef22312b",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "props": {
            "textColor": "default",
            "textAlignment": "left",
            "backgroundColor": "default"
          },
          "content": [
            {
              "text": "Scatter plot — reveals the relationship between two numeric variables. Use df.plot.scatter(x=\"a\",",
              "type": "text",
              "styles": {}
            }
          ],
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "id": "9bf04099-6526-4e68-a5d6-c29a3217f0e5",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "props": {
            "textColor": "default",
            "textAlignment": "left",
            "backgroundColor": "default"
          },
          "content": [
            {
              "text": "y=\"b\").",
              "type": "text",
              "styles": {}
            }
          ],
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "id": "887cdee8-90b0-4e31-8927-2bdab43232a0",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "props": {
            "textColor": "default",
            "textAlignment": "left",
            "backgroundColor": "default"
          },
          "content": [
            {
              "text": "Correlation matrix — df.corr() gives you the numbers; plt.imshow(df.corr()) renders the heatmap.",
              "type": "text",
              "styles": {}
            }
          ],
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "id": "2aae01fe-daa0-4f49-b0cf-b854925a5643",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "props": {
            "textColor": "default",
            "textAlignment": "left",
            "backgroundColor": "default"
          },
          "content": [
            {
              "text": "Bar chart — shows frequency counts for categorical variables. Use",
              "type": "text",
              "styles": {}
            }
          ],
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "id": "8ee9b3dc-7bb1-42a1-b7bc-95d8f22a975a",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "props": {
            "textColor": "default",
            "textAlignment": "left",
            "backgroundColor": "default"
          },
          "content": [
            {
              "text": "df[\"col\"].value_counts().plot.bar().",
              "type": "text",
              "styles": {}
            }
          ],
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "id": "828a4b23-bb5a-4d62-b0d7-4395d661ad73",
          "type": "heading",
          "props": {
            "level": 3,
            "textColor": "default",
            "isToggleable": false,
            "textAlignment": "left",
            "backgroundColor": "default"
          },
          "content": [
            {
              "text": "Quick-Look Helpers",
              "type": "text",
              "styles": {}
            }
          ],
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "id": "41288dd5-0a4c-458f-af4b-cb3a98afacfe",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "props": {
            "textColor": "default",
            "textAlignment": "left",
            "backgroundColor": "default"
          },
          "content": [
            {
              "text": "Before you plot, pandas gives you three one-liners worth memorizing:",
              "type": "text",
              "styles": {}
            }
          ],
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "id": "dc087392-e5d8-457a-8e01-262a68770d2a",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "props": {
            "textColor": "default",
            "textAlignment": "left",
            "backgroundColor": "default"
          },
          "content": [
            {
              "text": "df.head() — first five rows, to sanity-check the load.",
              "type": "text",
              "styles": {}
            }
          ],
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "id": "868af038-6567-4199-ad7b-1afe2e9f45ae",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "props": {
            "textColor": "default",
            "textAlignment": "left",
            "backgroundColor": "default"
          },
          "content": [
            {
              "text": "df.info() — column names, dtypes, non-null counts. Catches missing data fast.",
              "type": "text",
              "styles": {}
            }
          ],
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "id": "f6b9fcc5-69a6-4eea-bcb4-ca4de736486f",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "props": {
            "textColor": "default",
            "textAlignment": "left",
            "backgroundColor": "default"
          },
          "content": [
            {
              "text": "df.describe() — count, mean, std, min/max, and quartiles for every numeric column.",
              "type": "text",
              "styles": {}
            }
          ],
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "id": "856e38b9-71e9-464b-995c-eafa68924295",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "props": {
            "textColor": "default",
